this marks only"},{"attachments":{"media_keys":["3_2110348561401749504"]},"author_id":"961968439597256705","conversation_id":"2110348576761254030","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:34:43.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2110348576761254030"],"entities":{"urls":[{"display_url":"pic.x.com/GDApnzmKkp","end":294,"expanded_url":"https://x.com/Macrobysunil/status/2110348576761254030/photo/1","media_key":"3_2110348561401749504","start":271,"url":"https://t.co/GDApnzmKkp"}]},"id":"2110348576761254030","lang":"en","note_tweet":{"text":"Inflation comes in hotter than expected and the reaction is immediate.\n\nSeptember CPI: Headline: 3.7% YoY vs 3.6% expected\nCore: 2.6% YoY vs 2.5% expected\nCore MoM: +0.3% vs +0.2% expected\nHeadline MoM: +0.6%, in line with expectations. \n\nDollar and yields ripped higher immediately after the print:\n\nDXY +0.3% → 102.53\nUS 2Y +6 bps → 4.85%\nUS 10Y +4 bps → 5.26%\nUS 30Y +2 bps → 5.58%\nGold -0.86% → $4,125\n\nMore importantly, core inflation is reaccelerating — 2.6% YoY from 2.4% previously, while energy inflation is already running 20.4% YoY.\n\nThis is the environment where the bond market becomes the pressure point. Higher inflation → higher yields → stronger dollar → pressure across duration-sensitive assets."},"possibly_sensitive":false,"public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":5,"impression_count":7403,"like_count":77,"quote_count":1,"reply_count":9,"retweet_count":8},"text":"Inflation comes in hotter than expected and the reaction is immediate.\n\nSeptember CPI: Headline: 3.7% YoY vs 3.6% expected\nCore: 2.6% YoY vs 2.5% expected\nCore MoM: +0.3% vs +0.2% expected\nHeadline MoM: +0.6%, in line with expectations. \n\nDollar and yields ripped higher https://t.co/GDApnzmKkp"},{"attachments":{"media_keys":["3_2110386571803279360"]},"author_id":"22149757","conversation_id":"2110386772978897298","created_at":"2026-10-14T15:06:30.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2110386578686198188","2110386772978897298"],"entities":{"urls":[{"display_url":"pic.x.