{"id":"2110369976330633637","type":"replied_to"}],"text":"5/6 September CPI: +0.6% MoM / +3.7% YoY. Core: +0.3% / +2.6%.\n\nAfter the release, the U.S. 10Y jumped ~9 bp to 5.304% and DXY rose ~0.55% to 102.75.\n\nThat reaction followed CPI — so it cannot be cleanly assigned to Hormuz.\nhttps://t.co/W3UuDRDRrc"},{"attachments":{"media_keys":["3_2110352052102545409"]},"author_id":"1679591758332657665","conversation_id":"2110352739402162447","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:51:16.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2110352362598498783","2110352689464820082","2110352739402162447"],"entities":{"urls":[{"display_url":"pic.x.com/022DvK6QAZ","end":298,"expanded_url":"https://x.com/GlobalMktObserv/status/2110352739402162447/photo/1","media_key":"3_2110352052102545409","start":275,"url":"https://t.co/022DvK6QAZ"}]},"id":"2110352739402162447","lang":"en","note_tweet":{"text":"US INFLATION IS RUNNING HOTTER THAN EXPECTED:\n\nSeptember CPI rose +0.6% MoM, matching forecasts, while YoY inflation increased to +3.7% versus +3.6% expected, marking the 3rd-highest reading since September 2023.\n\nCore CPI increased +0.3% MoM against +0.2% expected, pushing annual core inflation to +2.6% from +2.45%, above the +2.5% forecast.\n\nThe unrounded figures were even hotter, with headline CPI rising +0.649% MoM versus +0.58% expected, while core CPI increased +0.335% against +0.21% forecast.\n\nEnergy costs drove more than half of the monthly CPI increase, as gasoline prices surged +9.1% and fuel oil, including diesel, jumped +15.3%.\n\nMarkets reacted sharply, with the Bloomberg Dollar Spot Index rising to its highest level since November and the 2-year Treasury yield jumping +13 basis points to 4.92%.\n\nAs a result, markets are increasing bets on 3 additional Fed rate hikes by the end of 2027, putting renewed monetary tightening firmly back on the table."},"possibly_sensitive":false,"public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":7,"impression_count":4024,"like_count":50,"quote_count":2,"reply_count":11,"retw